From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windowscodecs, gdiplus: a BMP as GDI+ writes it -- the file size with its colour table, 32-bit alpha bitmaps as BI_RGB (9463)

Image.Save(stream, ImageFormat.Bmp) is how PDFsharp (NAPS2, and many .NET programs that make PDFs) reads a bitmap's pixels: it saves the image as a BMP and checks the header -- bfSize equal to the stream's length, a 40-byte BITMAPINFOHEADER, BI_RGB, 32 bits for an image with alpha -- and refuses anything else with NotImplementedException ("ReadIndexedMemoryBitmap: unsupported format"). Wine's BMP encoder left the colour table out of bfSize (an indexed BMP's size was short by 4 bytes a colour), and GDI+ handed a 32bpp ARGB bitmap to WIC as 32bppBGRA, which writes a BITMAPV4HEADER with bit fields (and a PARGB bitmap fell back to 24 bits, its alpha lost). Windows' GDI+ writes a 32-bit BI_RGB BMP with a BITMAPINFOHEADER and the alpha in each pixel's fourth byte. NAPS2 6.1 could not save any page as PDF ("An error occurred when trying to save the file").

bmpencode.c: bfSize counts the colour table. gdiplus encode_frame_wic: for the BMP container a 32bpp (P)ARGB bitmap is written as 32bppBGR from ARGB bits (the alpha bytes kept).

Gate: test-gdipbmpsave (indexed 1/4/8bpp bfSize and offsets, 24bpp, 32bpp ARGB/PARGB header and alpha byte): 10.0-1185 5 FAIL, after 6/6. Mutants SG_MUTANT_BMP_SIZE_NO_PALETTE (bmpencode.c, 3 FAIL), SG_MUTANT_BMP_ALPHA_BITFIELDS (image.c, 2 FAIL).
---
--- a/dlls/gdiplus/image.c
+++ b/dlls/gdiplus/image.c
@@ -5024,6 +5024,20 @@
                 gdipformat = PixelFormat32bppARGB;
             }
 
+            /* Stained Glass OS: GDI+ saves a bitmap with alpha as a BMP of 32 bits with a
+             * BITMAPINFOHEADER and BI_RGB, the alpha kept in each pixel's fourth byte -- not
+             * WIC's BITMAPV4HEADER with bit fields. PDFsharp reads Image.Save(Bmp) expecting
+             * exactly that (NAPS2's PDF export of a colour page failed). */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_BMP_ALPHA_BITFIELDS
+            if (IsEqualGUID(&container_format, &GUID_ContainerFormatBmp) &&
+                (IsEqualGUID(desired_wicformat, &GUID_WICPixelFormat32bppBGRA) ||
+                 IsEqualGUID(desired_wicformat, &GUID_WICPixelFormat32bppPBGRA)))
+            {
+                desired_wicformat = &GUID_WICPixelFormat32bppBGR;
+                gdipformat = PixelFormat32bppARGB;
+            }
+#endif
+
             memcpy(&wicformat, desired_wicformat, sizeof(GUID));
             hr = IWICBitmapFrameEncode_SetPixelFormat(frameencode, &wicformat);
         }
--- a/dlls/windowscodecs/bmpencode.c
+++ b/dlls/windowscodecs/bmpencode.c
@@ -385,6 +385,12 @@
     bfh.bfSize = sizeof(BITMAPFILEHEADER) + info_size + bih.bV5SizeImage;
     bfh.bfOffBits = sizeof(BITMAPFILEHEADER) + info_size;
     bfh.bfOffBits += bih.bV5ClrUsed * sizeof(WICColor);
+    /* Stained Glass OS: the file's size counts the colour table too, as Windows writes it
+     * (PDFsharp checks bfSize against the stream: NAPS2 could not save a black-and-white or
+     * greyscale page as PDF) */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_BMP_SIZE_NO_PALETTE
+    bfh.bfSize += bih.bV5ClrUsed * sizeof(WICColor);
+#endif
 
     pos.QuadPart = 0;
     hr = IStream_Seek(This->stream, pos, STREAM_SEEK_SET, NULL);
